# Styling and theming

- Core has no Tailwind or UnoCSS dependency.
- Public theme variables use the `--dui-` prefix.
- Prefer semantic CSS variables such as control background, text, border and focus colors over hard-coded palette values.
- Component styles consume theme tokens; they do not own global theme policy.
- Dark/light modes must be expressed through token values.
- Keep selectors shallow and avoid global leakage.
- Do not encode behavior in class names.
- Interactive states should be observable through attributes where useful: `data-disabled`, `data-active`, `data-loading`, etc.
